            [
                'title' => 'Notifications and Account Alerts',
                'summary' => 'Turn alerts into a habit that keeps you informed.',
                'duration' => 30,
                'content' => "The platform sends notifications for a reason: verification updates, wallet movements, program deadlines, and messages. Growers who read their alerts stay ahead; growers who ignore them are surprised by things they could have seen coming.\n\nStart by enabling the notifications that matter: wallet alerts, document status changes, and program announcements. These are the three that affect your money and your access, and each one is time-sensitive. A document rejection answered the same day is a rejection fixed in minutes; one answered in a month is a missed program.\n\nKnow what each alert means before it arrives. A wallet alert shows a hold, a release, or a completed movement; a document alert shows pending, under review, verified, or rejected; a program alert opens a window. The grower who knows the vocabulary of alerts reads them in seconds and acts on the one that needs action.\n\nCheck the notification centre regularly, even when nothing seems to be happening. Some alerts are quiet: a program opening, a coverage change, a deadline reminder. The grower who checks weekly catches the quiet ones, and the quiet ones are often the most valuable.\n\nFinally, keep your contact details current, because every alert depends on them. A phone that cannot receive messages is a farm the platform cannot reach. The grower who keeps alerts on, reads them, and keeps their contacts current is the grower who is never the last to know.",
