            [
                'title' => 'The Story Your Data Tells',
                'summary' => 'Read the registry like a report card.',
                'duration' => 30,
                'content' => "Your registry record is more than facts; it is a report card the cooperative reads to decide who to serve first. Understanding what your data says about you helps you tell the story you want.\n\nStart with completeness. A profile with verified phone, verified documents, and current farm details is a profile the programs can trust. Every verified field is a green tick in a reviewer's mind, and green ticks are what get growers selected for input programs, financing, and premium markets.\n\nNext, read the activity. A record with recent updates, recent verifications, and recent transactions is an active farm. Programs look for activity because active farms respond, deliver, and participate. A record that has not changed in two years reads as a farm that may no longer exist, however good the harvest is.\n\nThen read the history. Your past verifications, payments, and program participation are your reputation in data form. A grower with a history of verified visits and clean transactions is a grower the cooperative can vouch for, and vouches are what open doors.\n\nFinally, improve the story deliberately. Update the stale fields, verify the unverified phone, and keep the record active. The registry is written in your name, but the story is written by what you keep current. The grower who curates the record curates the opportunities.",
