                'content' => "Registry quality is a shared harvest. One grower with a duplicate profile is a small error; a whole LGA with duplicates is a data problem that misroutes field visits and delays payments for everyone. The grower who helps neighbours fix their records raises the quality of the entire area.\n\nStart with the common errors: duplicate accounts, wrong state or LGA, unverified phones, and stale contacts. Learn to spot them in your own record first, because the grower who has fixed their own errors speaks with authority when they help a neighbour.\n\nTeach the fix, not just the problem. Show a neighbour how to report a duplicate through the support desk, how to select state and LGA from the dropdowns, and how to re-verify a phone. The fix taught once is the fix used for years, and the neighbour who learns the fix becomes the next teacher.\n\nEncourage the monthly ten-minute check: read your record, correct the stale fields, confirm the contacts. A habit shared is a habit kept, and a group of growers who check monthly is an LGA whose data stays clean without a campaign.\n\nFinally, report patterns, not just individual errors. If several farms in one area have wrong LGAs, tell the support desk; that is a registry defect worth fixing for everyone. The grower who reports the pattern fixes the system, and the system is what every grower depends on.",
