            [
                'title' => 'Your First Weeks as a Provider',
                'summary' => 'Build the store\'s routines from day one.',
                'duration' => 30,
                'content' => "Accreditation is the start of the business on the platform, and your first weeks set the routines that decide whether the store grows or stalls. The provider who builds good routines early wins the marketplace without a marketing budget.\n\nStart with the daily routine: check inquiries, check stock, and update listings before noon. A store that answers within the day outsells a store that answers within the week, and the morning check is what makes the fast answer possible. The routine is boring; the results are not.\n\nNext, build the fulfilment routine: confirm orders, pack to a standard, and dispatch with a photo. Every order should end the same way: the right product, confirmed in the platform, with evidence of dispatch. The routine is what makes the second order easier than the first, and the tenth easier than the second.\n\nKeep the records routine: what sold, what was asked, and what ran out. A weekly ten-minute review of the store's activity shows the patterns: the product that always sells, the inquiry that repeats, the listing that never converts. The provider who reads the patterns stocks the right things.\n\nFinally, build the learning routine. Ask your best customers what they need, watch what competitors list well, and fix your weakest listing each week. The provider whose first weeks are routine-driven is the provider whose tenth month is profitable.",
