                'content' => "Every provider's first complaint is a fork in the road: handled well, it creates a loyal customer; handled badly, it creates a bad review that follows the store for months. The difference is not the complaint; it is the response.\n\nStart by listening and acknowledging. Read the complaint fully before replying, and acknowledge the problem in your own words. The customer who feels heard is already halfway to satisfied, and the provider who acknowledges first is the provider who resolves fastest. Never argue with the customer's experience; it is their experience.\n\nNext, fix what can be fixed: replace the product, refund through the platform, or correct the order. Offer the remedy clearly and do it through the platform, where the record is clean. A refund handled through the platform is a refund both sides can see, and a clear remedy is a closed complaint.\n\nThen find the cause. Was it the product, the listing, the packing, or the delivery? The complaint that is fixed once is a service recovery; the complaint that keeps repeating is a business problem. Fix the cause, not just the case, and note it in your store's improvement list.\n\nFinally, follow up. A short message after the remedy, asking whether the customer is satisfied, turns a complaint into loyalty. The provider who handles the first complaint well is the provider whose reviews stay strong, because every store has complaints; only some stores handle them.",
