                'content' => "Programs run on calendars, and the grower who aligns the farm with the program calendar gets the inputs early, the programs funded, and the harvests sold. Timing is the free advantage that planning buys.\n\nStart with the farm calendar: planting windows, fertiliser windows, harvest months, and the dry spells that stress young palms. Write them down for your blocks, because a farm calendar in your head is a plan you forget, and a calendar on paper is a plan you can check.\n\nNext, learn the program calendar: when input programs open, when financing applications close, and when field visits are scheduled. Ask your field agent for the dates for your area, and mark them on the same calendar as the farm windows. The grower who sees both calendars together applies before the rush, and the early application is the funded one.\n\nAlign purchases with the windows. Inputs ordered before the planting window arrive before the rush and at the listed price; inputs ordered in the panic week cost more and arrive late. The calendar turns a reactive season into a planned one.\n\nFinally, review the calendar each season and correct it. Last season's dates are the best forecast for this season's. The grower who keeps the farm and program calendars together is the grower who is never surprised, and the un-surprised grower is the one who harvests on time.",
